# Deny by default, allow by exception.
#
# Everything is ignored unless re-included below, so a new file is invisible to
# git until someone adds it here deliberately. Nothing rides along into a
# published repository by accident - no editor backups, no caches, no scratch
# files, no local notes, no captured data.
#
# Re-including a directory is not enough on its own: git descends into an
# allowed directory, so each one needs its own "exclude everything, then allow
# the file type" pair. Adding a new kind of file means editing this file, which
# is the point.

# --- repository root: nothing but these
/*
!/.gitignore
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/README_EN.md
!/template/

# --- the template itself: the export only
/template/*
!/template/*.yaml
